WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.236 --> 00:00:03.236
(soft somber music)

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.690
- [Narrator] When the
coronavirus first arrived

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.370
in the United States, few
places were hit as hard

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.450
as nursing homes, and few
nursing homes were hit as hard

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.760
as the Menlo Park Veterans Memorial Home

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.023
in central New Jersey.

00:00:17.592 --> 00:00:19.810
A "Wall Street Journal"
investigation found

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.980
that nearly 100 people
died at Menlo in April,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.523
more than 10 times the
number in a typical month.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.520
A spokesman for the state
agency that runs Menlo

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.160
declined to respond to most
of the "Journal's" questions,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.940
citing expected litigation, but in August,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.470
reporter Chris Weaver
interviewed Vietnam veteran

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.860
and surviving resident Glenn Osbourne

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.820
to understand more about what happened

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.613
to the residents of Menlo Park.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.780
- Now that we're nearly six months out

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.807
from the beginnings of the pandemic,

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:52.650
do you feel like you know the status

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.220
of all the residents who you
knew before the outbreak began?

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.040
- I would say 85% I know.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.420
There's a few I don't know

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.120
and I would like to know
of a couple residents

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.763
that I knew socially where they are.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:13.800
Recently, even though I'm
not supposed to wander out,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.480
I've gone out and I would find them.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.430
They're so weak.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.883
They can hardly talk.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.670
And they're so pale and they're not moving

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.443
and they're still trying to
recover from this disease.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.053
It's a horrible thing to see.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.370
- [Narrator] Among the dead
were 84-year-old Isabella Kovacs

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.780
and 86-year-old Joan Williams.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.300
Their stories provide a window

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.453
into what went wrong at Menlo Park.

00:01:42.316 --> 00:01:45.233
(soft piano music)

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.660
The Menlo Park Memorial Veterans Home

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:54.083
accepts veterans, their
spouses, and Gold Star parents.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.830
It has 312 beds in six residential units,

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.810
all with patriotic names:

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.800
Stars and Stripes, where
the dementia patients lived,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.453
and Freedom, where Joan lived.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.100
Joan moved to Menlo in 2015.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.270
She was elected to be representative
to the resident council

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.150
for about three years running.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.790
- She would travel up and down the hallway

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:22.240
of Freedom, talking to the residents,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.370
asking what is their concerns?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:28.913
Heh, that can go on for a
half hour at a time sometimes.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.340
- We would go to visit her

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.340
and even family members of other residents

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.490
knew my mother on a first name basis.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.090
She always had her makeup
together, her hair done,

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:46.290
and you know, just a classy type of lady.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.520
- [Narrator] Isabella
Kovacs arrived at Menlo Park

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.280
in January 2020.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.100
She had served in both the
Army and the Air Force.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.850
- Like Joan, she was in the Freedom unit.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.630
- Once we got here, they had a welcome,

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.250
a little room that had a big sign

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.850
that said welcome on a chalkboard

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.260
and they had a balloon for her

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.263
and they brought us all beverages
and offered us some lunch.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.593
- [Narrator] But she would
have little time to settle in.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.470
Not long after Isabella
arrived, there was an outbreak

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.360
in the Life Care Nursing
Home in Kirkland, Washington,

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.540
and soon after, the coronavirus
began spreading rapidly

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.110
in nursing homes around the country.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.667
Still, Menlo was caught
flat-footed by the outbreak

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.440
and the administration's best attempts

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.220
to mitigate the spread fell short.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.840
They created a quarantine
area for COVID patients

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.030
within the Alzheimer's
unit, Stars and Stripes.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.630
It was separated from the rest of the unit

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.550
with a plastic tarp.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.260
And the home resisted other
more obvious safety measures.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.399
- One of the things that
we keep hearing about

00:03:45.399 --> 00:03:49.250
is that the staff weren't
wearing protective equipment

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.850
all the time and, in
fact, that it sounds like

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.490
the administration might
have instructed them not to

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:55.510
for some reason.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.343
- Yes.

00:03:56.343 --> 00:04:00.470
I actually witnessed senior administration

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.680
physically remove the protective equipment

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.660
from the storage cabinet.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.620
They were said, "We
don't want you to wear it

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.020
because you'll frighten the residents,"

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.890
and that frightened me more than anything.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.940
- [Narrator] Staff members
claim they were not allowed

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.403
to wear masks outside the quarantine unit.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.120
A March 27th email from
the New Jersey Department

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.670
of Veterans Affairs to Menlo's CEO

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:26.700
outlined the escalating consequences

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.756
for mask insubordination, oral counseling,

00:04:29.756 --> 00:04:34.063
written warning, official
reprimand, and suspension.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.060
Menlo spokesmen declined to comment,

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.210
but Brigadier General Mark Piterski,

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.490
who was deputy director
of the agency at the time

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.586
but has since retired, said
masks were in short supply

00:04:44.586 --> 00:04:48.083
and the agency was following
federal guidelines.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:54.230
Joan and Isabella's story takes
a turn in the end of March.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.290
- I spoke to her on a regular basis.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.650
I spoke to the nurse supervisor.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.883
She was doing fine. She was doing fine.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.620
- [Narrator] On March 30th,
Menlo resident Rose Dente

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.460
tested positive for the
virus at an emergency room

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.440
at a nearby hospital.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.342
She died the next day.

00:05:11.342 --> 00:05:13.920
The virus was inside Menlo Park,

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.168
but the administration didn't
tell residents' families.

00:05:17.168 --> 00:05:21.830
- April 3rd is when I lost
communication with my mom.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:25.325
The 4th, still can't
get in touch with Mom.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:27.740
The 5th, can't get in touch
with the nurses' station,

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.466
can't get in touch with Mom.

00:05:29.466 --> 00:05:31.960
- [Narrator] Joan was
somewhere on the Freedom unit.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.020
A few days after Sheri lost track of her,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:38.610
she was put into room 239
alongside Isabella Kovacs.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:41.260
- It was obvious by
then Joan was very sick.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.590
She was asleep all the
time and they were in there

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.900
checking her temperature
all day long she said.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.050
The staff wouldn't tell me anything.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.090
- [Narrator] but in an April 6th email,

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.440
the home's CEO, Elizabeth Schiff-Heedles,

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.160
asked for permission to tell residents

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:57.349
and their family members
that COVID was spreading.

00:05:57.349 --> 00:05:59.220
The next day, April 7th,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.680
she mailed that letter,
but more than a week

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.330
after the first resident tested
positive for coronavirus.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.330
It was too late for Joan.

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.680
She was transferred to Room
753 in Stars and Stripes

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.040
and, later that night, to the hospital.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.243
- Mom tested positive for COVID.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.960
Her lungs were in very bad condition.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.723
So it was like a perfect storm.

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:24.690
- [Narrator] Back at Menlo,
Isabella was getting sick.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.760
She, too, was transferred
somewhere in Stars and Stripes.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.610
- I asked three different staff members

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.792
if they were gonna test her for COVID

00:06:31.792 --> 00:06:35.207
and all three said, "We
don't test for COVID here."

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:39.550
On April 12th, well into
the outbreak at Menlo,

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.380
the New Jersey Department of
Military and Veterans Affairs

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.830
posted this video on Facebook.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.880
It shows the staff and CEO
of the home, Schiff-Heedles,

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.820
dancing in the hallways
in an apparent effort

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.360
to raise the residents' spirits.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.740
Menlo declined to comment.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:59.053
- They trying to say
they're trying to cheer up.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.300
I was in shock.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.620
They were dancing in the hallways

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.150
where, literally, the residents were dying

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.423
in the rooms that they were passing by.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.740
- [Narrator] Plastic sheets
separating Stars and Stripes

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.076
from the rest of the facility was sagging.

00:07:15.076 --> 00:07:18.900
Staff members in full
PPE went back and forth

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.430
across the partition.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:21.580
More and more residents

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.280
were being shuffled throughout the home.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:27.340
Isabella was sent to the
emergency room on April 17th

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.670
and also tested positive for COVID.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.063
She and Joan were dying.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:33.640
- They let me go on up.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.840
I put on two masks and a face shield.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.700
I had two pairs of gloves.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.320
I told her about heaven

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:43.513
and I listed the names of
everybody she's gonna see again.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.970
I told her that she was the best mother

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:50.293
I've ever could have had
and how much I loved her

00:07:50.293 --> 00:07:53.380
and that she's gonna get this mask off

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.543
and she's gonna fly free.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:08:01.683
And I couldn't stay in there
that long because I was just,

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.830
I didn't want her to just hear me cry.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.710
I was just trying not to.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:09.540
- And then the nurse knocked on the door

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.740
and I told her, I said, "Mom, I love you."

00:08:16.692 --> 00:08:21.253
And that's the last (sniffles)

00:08:21.253 --> 00:08:22.983
that I was with my mother.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.490
- Unfortunately, both passed away

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.830
within a couple of days of one another.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.130
I wanted to share those details with you

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.890
only because it does seem like,

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:35.570
you know, her particular path,
- Path.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.310
- kind of covered some of the same ground

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.950
that we were speaking
about generally earlier.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.530
- Means a lot to me. I appreciate it.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.530
Thank you.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:45.390
- [Narrator] Joan Williams
died on April 21st.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:48.840
Isabella Kovacs died on April 23rd.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.550
Their families are among those
that have begun the process

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.713
of suing the agency that runs Menlo.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.200
The agency reported just 62
deaths in its official tally.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.870
A spokesman said that count

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.042
is based on experts' conclusions

00:09:03.042 --> 00:09:05.340
and that the agency mourns the loss

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.473
of every veteran at its facilities.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.790
But dozens more died
with COVID-like symptoms,

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.080
according to internal patient records.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.010
Many of those residents were never tested,

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:15.993
their families say.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.470
The New Jersey Department of Health

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.830
ultimately confirmed the
"Journal's" findings,

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:24.770
revealing another 39 probable
COVID deaths at Menlo.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:28.943
- I have lost more friends,
more good veterans,

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.553
than I did in the war and combat.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.803
These are true heroes.

00:09:36.661 --> 00:09:38.843
They fought for America.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:44.120
They were wounded soldiers and came back,

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:48.010
came back from World War
II and Korea and Vietnam,

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:53.010
only to be left here and
treated with indignity,

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:56.398
not cared for, not protected.

00:09:56.398 --> 00:09:59.398
(soft somber music)

